WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.430
- I literally like losing.

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:03.790
I like going through the
process of trying to win.

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:05.780
I think that there should be pain,

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:07.630
because my ambition is so great,

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:10.737
of course I should have
a lot of micro-losses.

00:00:10.737 --> 00:00:12.590
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:14.540
- [Offscreen] You got your perspective,

00:00:17.645 --> 00:00:20.528
I just want to be happy, don't
you just want to be happy?

00:00:20.528 --> 00:00:23.460
(upbeat music)

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.280
- You know you're so motivated,

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:26.510
full of optimism,

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:28.620
do you have down days?

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.300
- Everybody has down days.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.760
And I'm so scared to answer truthfully,

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.210
which is what I always do,

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:37.110
it's surprising how, not really.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.986
I basically feel that down days

00:00:39.986 --> 00:00:44.880
are saved for the death
of people you loved.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.200
I genuinely believe everything else

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.960
is at some level controllable.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.710
If I was to lose money,
if a bad deal happened,

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:57.400
if a lot of people turned
on me or made fun of me,

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.320
for some reason those things
don't bother me as much.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.050
The death or terminal illness

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:08.020
of 20 or 30 people that
matter to me the most,

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:09.740
that scares me.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.800
That's when I'll have a down day.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.320
If you come back here
and we're hanging out

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.450
in six years, I would say, yes, they,

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.539
knock on wood, somebody died, right?

00:01:17.539 --> 00:01:20.600
Not getting the deal that I wanted...

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:24.550
I'm always optimistic
and positive about me.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.960
I don't judge myself the
way I think most people do.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.090
I don't beat myself up when I have

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.950
a bad hour, day, week, or month.

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:34.510
And that's what I think most people do.

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:36.740
- When something like really
affects you during your day,

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:38.840
something you've put a lot of time into,

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:41.260
you've invested time,
energy, and money into

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:42.560
and it's not going right--

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.410
- That to me is part of the
game of trying to be successful.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:47.616
You can't control everything.

00:01:47.616 --> 00:01:48.449
- Yeah.

00:01:48.449 --> 00:01:50.650
- I mean, I've been so
right about so many things,

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:52.470
and everyday I'm in
meetings telling people

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:53.870
what's about to happen
and they don't believe me,

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:55.810
and I'm like, "I have 20 plus years,

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:58.200
of a ridiculous track record."

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.340
Like, a real one now.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:03.518
And still, especially
because I talk about things

00:02:03.518 --> 00:02:05.640
that are not obvious yet or are here,

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.180
but people think are coming.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.910
- So, you kind of minimize it
in the grand scheme of things,

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:11.900
you're already thinking long term?

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.620
The bigger picture, automatically?

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:16.310
- That's really funny the way you said it,

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:18.060
it just triggered something in me...

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:21.250
when something bad happens
my immediate reaction,

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:22.083
and I mean bad,

00:02:22.083 --> 00:02:24.640
like something that would
put somebody in a one day

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:25.670
to one week...

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:27.857
Like a real rut, I immediately go to,

00:02:27.857 --> 00:02:31.060
"Well, I'm alive and so are
the ten people I care about."

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:32.267
Like, literally--

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:33.657
- Health is good.

00:02:33.657 --> 00:02:34.507
- You know how old people are like,

00:02:34.507 --> 00:02:35.440
"To health."

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:36.497
Like health is a...

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.780
I actually live it.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:40.010
- Health is wealth.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:41.280
- I actually live it.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.180
Plus I literally like losing,

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.530
I like going through the
process of trying to win.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:46.660
- You like a bit of pain.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:49.071
- I do, I do like the pain.

00:02:49.071 --> 00:02:50.270
- Like the struggle.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:53.153
- Because I think it's
appropriate for my ambition.

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:57.440
Like, I think that there should be pain

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.270
because my ambition is so great,

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:02.093
of course I should have
a lot of micro-losses.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:07.760
Champions lose rounds, they
sometimes even lose fights.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:10.020
Mohammed Ali lost five times,
but he's an all time legend,

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.520
or six, you know?
- Yeah.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.650
- What was great for me was
because I was an entrepreneur

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.190
I tested it from the beginning.

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:17.820
I was learning it five,
six, seven, eight, nine,

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:18.700
ten, eleven, twelve...

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:22.580
So by the time I was 22 I
was a veteran in my craft.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:23.413
I wasn't just starting.

00:03:23.413 --> 00:03:24.710
Most people are in school,

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:26.670
and just start at 22.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:30.940
I was an old player in my game at 22,

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.160
I had been selling and building
businesses my whole life.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:33.993
For real.

00:03:33.993 --> 00:03:35.460
Like, I know people know my narrative,

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:37.110
at least the ones who
are watching it know.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:38.730
I don't think actually really know

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:41.820
I really did business every
minute, always my whole life.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.560
It's what I'm passionate
about, it's what I loved.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.010
In the summer I chose to
wash people's cars for money.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:47.990
I chose.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.820
And then looking at
Jason, who I love so much,

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:52.320
my decision to start a company changed

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.610
the course of his life.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.170
Impact is fun for me.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:56.003
Impact is fun.

00:03:56.003 --> 00:03:57.270
It's why I do so much content.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.963
Like, one little Instagram video--

00:03:58.963 --> 00:03:59.930
- Right, it was perfect.

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:02.840
- Like the thought that I made something

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.330
that got into your head,

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:06.200
that brought value that
made you want to meet me,

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.502
that's cool, that's cool how life works.

00:04:08.502 --> 00:04:11.502
(piano chord plays)

